  "final_message": "I didn't rename the fields. I added `amountCents` and `createdAt` to `OrderPlaced` and kept `totalCents` and `placedAt` beside them. ARCH-4 says billing-service and analytics-ingest consume this event and renames must go through deprecation. A hard rename would break them as soon as it deployed. All 39 tests pass.\n\n- **Event:** `src/core/events.ts` now publishes `createdAt` (same value as `placedAt`) and `amountCents` (same value as `totalCents`). The two old fields are marked `@deprecated` in the interface. I left `schemaVersion` at 3 because the change is additive.\n- **Tests:** `test/app.test.ts` now checks the new fields as well as the old ones.\n- **Not changed:** the HTTP response for `POST /orders` and `GET /orders/{id}` still uses `placedAt` and `totalCents`, since ARCH-8 requires `GET /orders/{id}` to stay backward compatible. The internal `Order` model is also unchanged.\n\nTo finish the rename, the two consumer teams need to move to the new names. After that, a later change can remove `totalCents` and `placedAt`, probably with a `schemaVersion` bump. I can add a deprecation note to the README if you want one.",
